WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.613
- Three, two, one, see ya.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.640
Base jumping is already the most

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.607
dangerous sport in the world.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.440
Ah!

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.140
Then you're also mixing that
with big mountain skiing.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.540
You're combining full intensity sports

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.180
in an unforgiving environment.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.280
The risk factor is definitely pretty high.

00:00:18.778 --> 00:00:21.361
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.254 --> 00:00:28.150
I am Matthias Giraud, aka Super Frenchie.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.120
I'm a pro big mountain skier
and professional base jumper,

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.310
and I like to put those
two sports together.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.760
Ski base jumping is
skiing off a massive cliff

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.790
that would be too big to
survive and land safely.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.800
So you use a parachute.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.570
I like to use my parachute
as a tool to ski things

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.550
that otherwise could not ski.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.150
I've been ski base jumping for 10 years

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.050
and the last 10 years have been filled

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.980
with a lot of fun adventures.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.470
I'm gonna ski between the rocks

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.630
and then jump into the event.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.500
I ski base jumped off of the Eiger

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.900
and also the Matterhorn in Switzerland.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.433
Heaven's Eleven in Telluride.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.550
I outran an avalanche by ski base jumping

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.903
off a 600-foot cliff.

00:01:07.011 --> 00:01:08.830
Woo hoo!
That was a pretty cool day.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.233
Did you see that avalanche?
Woo!

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.980
Fear is an interesting thing.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.147
Your instinct tells you,
"OK, stop right there,

00:01:18.147 --> 00:01:19.197
"don't go any further,

00:01:19.197 --> 00:01:20.777
"this is the end of the world right there,

00:01:20.777 --> 00:01:22.260
"this thing is gonna kill you."

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.290
This is the moment when
you have to take over

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:26.920
and be, "No, I'm gonna
jump off this thing."

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.630
And then you come flying off this cliff,

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.500
things get even faster and gnarlier,

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.280
then the ground is coming straight at you,

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.771
it feels like it's gonna eat you then.

00:01:34.771 --> 00:01:35.604
God!

00:01:37.494 --> 00:01:38.327
Aha!

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.020
The moment you land, oh
man, I love that time.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.600
Turn back, look at where you came from

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.887
and then realize that something
super cool just happened.

00:01:48.887 --> 00:01:51.139
(laughs)

00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:51.972
Oh fuck!

00:01:51.972 --> 00:01:54.340
Big mountain skiing base
jumping is not forgiving,

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.720
I've definitely lost a lot
of friends over the years.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.653
I've almost died myself several times.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.810
You gotta be on it; you
gotta do the right thing

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:03.860
if you want to do it for a long time.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.630
Oh, that was a terrifying jump.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.110
That was a close call, but, hey,

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:12.860
I'm alive, I'm not hurt, we did it.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.050
We're all looking for happiness,

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.610
and some people find happiness

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.540
through balance and monotony
and routine in their life,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.240
and for me, that's honestly
my worst nightmare.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.433
I seek happiness through intensity.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.570
I think that intensity can
bring the best out of people.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:29.403
Aha!

